---
import { GITHUB_URL, QUICKSTART } from "../lib/site.js";
---

<section class="noise-overlay relative overflow-hidden px-6 pt-32 pb-20 sm:pt-40 sm:pb-28">
  <div class="hero-glow pointer-events-none absolute inset-x-0 top-0 h-[36rem]"></div>

  <div class="relative z-10 mx-auto max-w-4xl text-center">
    <!-- No status dot. A pulsing dot is the universal gesture for "live", and
         this states a fact about the design rather than a state, so the dot was
         promising something that does not exist. -->
    <p
      class="animate-fade-in-up opacity-0-initial bg-accent text-on-accent text-label-md inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-pill px-3.5 py-1.5 font-mono uppercase"
      style="animation-delay: 80ms"
    >
      Open source · audit every line
    </p>

    <h1
      class="animate-fade-in-up opacity-0-initial mt-7 text-[32px] leading-[1.06] font-semibold tracking-[-1.2px] sm:text-[46px] lg:text-[56px]"
      style="animation-delay: 160ms"
    >
      <span class="text-gradient-accent">Secure execution for AI agents,</span><br />
      <span class="text-foreground-muted">on any machine</span>
    </h1>

    <p
      class="animate-fade-in-up opacity-0-initial text-body-lg text-foreground-muted mx-auto mt-6 max-w-2xl sm:text-[17px]"
      style="animation-delay: 240ms"
    >
      Connect any MCP client to the development environment on any machine you can run a command
      on: a server, a VM, a build box, a Raspberry Pi, or your own laptop. No port to open, no
      source code to upload, no tunnel to wire up. The whole stack is public - audit it, fork it,
      contribute.
    </p>

    <div
      class="animate-fade-in-up opacity-0-initial mt-10 flex flex-col items-center justify-center gap-3 sm:flex-row"
      style="animation-delay: 320ms"
    >
      <a
        href="/dashboard/"
        class="bg-accent text-on-accent hover:bg-foreground text-title-md w-full rounded-lg px-5 py-2.5 transition-colors duration-fast sm:w-auto"
      >
        Get started
      </a>
      <a
        href={GITHUB_URL}
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener"
        class="border-border text-foreground-muted hover:text-foreground hover:border-foreground-faint/30 text-title-md w-full rounded-lg border px-5 py-2.5 transition-colors duration-fast sm:w-auto"
      >
        Star on GitHub
      </a>
    </div>

    <!-- One command. It signs in, registers the machine and registers the
         directory only when those are missing, so there is nothing to run
         before it and nothing to read first. -->
    <div
      class="animate-fade-in-up opacity-0-initial border-border bg-surface mx-auto mt-12 flex max-w-xl items-center gap-3 rounded-xl border py-3 pr-3 pl-4 text-left"
      style="animation-delay: 400ms"
    >
      <!-- The `$` prompt is drawn with ::before so it stays out of
           textContent, and copying yields a runnable command. -->
      <code
        id="hero-quickstart"
        class="text-foreground before:text-foreground-faint min-w-0 flex-1 truncate font-mono text-[13px] before:content-['$_'] before:select-none sm:text-[15px]"
        >{QUICKSTART}</code
      >
      <button
        type="button"
        data-copy-target="hero-quickstart"
        class="text-label-md text-foreground-muted hover:text-foreground border-border hover:border-foreground-faint/30 shrink-0 rounded-md border px-2.5 py-1.5 font-mono transition-colors duration-fast"
      >
        <span data-copy-label>Copy</span>
      </button>
    </div>

    <p
      class="animate-fade-in-up opacity-0-initial text-body-md text-foreground-faint mt-4"
      style="animation-delay: 460ms"
    >
      Run it in the directory you want to serve. It signs you in and registers the machine on the
      way
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
